WEBVTT

2.1.1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.825
A coding-agent score belongs to a model, a harness, a task set, and an evaluation protocol.

2.1.2
00:00:07.125 --> 00:00:15.625
SWE-bench separates its all-agent leaderboard from a bash-only model comparison using mini-SWE-agent.

2.1.3
00:00:15.925 --> 00:00:22.075
The agent harness does the work; the evaluation harness sets up tasks and grades results.

2.2.1
00:00:23.175 --> 00:00:35.325
On Terminal-Bench 2.0, the official board lists GPT-5.2 at 62.9% with Codex CLI and 54.0% with Terminus 2.

2.2.2
00:00:35.625 --> 00:00:40.800
That compares systems, not harnesses with matched budgets across every task.

2.3.1
00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:53.475
The October 8, 2026 snapshot of Terminal-Bench 4.0 lists Opus 5.5 in Claude Code first, at 64.8%.

2.3.2
00:00:53.775 --> 00:01:01.650
SWE-bench Pro v2 has 642 public tasks and a separate HARD-51 subset.

2.3.3
00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:06.775
Changed tasks and protocols make a shared ranking axis misleading.

2.3.4
00:01:07.075 --> 00:01:13.875
The new terminal release repaired tasks, revised resource limits, and removed saturated problems.

2.4.1
00:01:14.975 --> 00:01:24.375
The peer-reviewed UTBoost study uncovered 345 erroneous patches that passed the original SWE-bench tests.

2.4.2
00:01:24.675 --> 00:01:31.400
Those findings changed historical Lite and Verified rankings; they do not describe today's standings.

2.5.1
00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:41.625
Validity cuts both ways: weak tests accept bad fixes, while overly specific tests or broken environments reject good ones.

2.5.2
00:01:41.925 --> 00:01:49.075
The peer-reviewed Agentic Benchmark Checklist separates task validity, outcome validity, and reporting.

2.5.3
00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:57.075
AI Agents That Matter recommends cost alongside accuracy and protected holdouts; HAL charts those trade-offs.

2.6.1
00:01:58.175 --> 00:02:06.700
METR's time horizon measures task difficulty in human time at a chosen success probability, not agent runtime.

2.6.2
00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:12.475
Its clean, self-contained tasks differ from a familiar employee's everyday work.

2.7.1
00:02:13.575 --> 00:02:24.150
Composio reports omp completing 17 of 30 SaaS workflows with DeepSeek V4 Flash, not a flagship coding-board result.

2.7.2
00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:31.050
Its Pi comparison changes reasoning settings and providers, limiting harness-only conclusions.

2.7.3
00:02:31.350 --> 00:02:40.300
Hermes and DeepSeek Harness appear in an independent preprint; Pi and DeepSeek Harness also appear in DeepSeek's own evaluation.

2.7.4
00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:49.300
The Hermes Index compares models within Hermes, excludes GPU tasks from its terminal suite, and flags provisional results.

2.7.5
00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:54.900
Read the system and protocol before treating a passing score as capability.
